We are proud to announce the first public beta release (0.9) of the  
OpenPanel project. OpenPanel is an open source remote server  
administration tool with both an AJAX GUI and a powerful command line  
interface. This first release focuses on getting the basic  
functionality up for managing a typical web hosting server with  
configuration for users, dns, email, websites and related services.  
The OpenPanel architecture is designed with extendability in mind,  
with a fully modular lay-out that allows extra modules to be written  
in any language under the sun.

This beta release supports the following distributions in ready-to- 
install package formats:
- CentOS 4
- Debian Etch

The Debian packages appear to also work on Ubuntu 6.10 and up and  
packaging efforts are under way to support Fedora Core 8.

Screenshots, documentation and download instructions can be found on  
our website at:

     http://www.openpanel.com/

- The OpenPanel Team

